# Next.js Stack

## Framework

- Next.js App Router only — never Pages Router (`pages/`, `getServerSideProps`, `getStaticProps`).
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when needed (state, effects, browser APIs).
- File-based routing: `app/layout.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- Route handlers in `app/api/` for API endpoints.
- `next/image` for images; metadata for SEO; env vars for config.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode; avoid `any`, prefer `unknown` with runtime checks.
- Explicit types for function inputs/outputs.
- `interface` for extendable shapes; `type` for unions/intersections.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS utility classes; avoid custom CSS unless necessary.
- shadcn/ui for UI primitives — import from `@/components/ui/`.
- Responsive variants; consistent utility class order.
- Source files in `src/` when using src directory layout.

## Code Quality

- Readable code over micro-optimizations.
- Implement fully — no TODOs, placeholders, or missing pieces.
- Minimize scope: only change what's needed for the task.
- Reuse existing components and patterns before creating new ones.
- Accessible and responsive by default.

## Deployment

- Compatible with Vercel hosting.
